hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17748","Waki narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to me, from Khaythama ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father who said: The name of my father in the pre-Islamic age was Aziz, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named him Abd al-Rahman."
"17749","Waki narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Khaythama ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the best of your names are Abdullah and Abd al-Rahman."
"17750","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abu Waki narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Khaythama ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sabra, that his father Abd al-Rahman went with his grandfather to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What is the name of your son. He said: Aziz. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not name him Aziz, but name him Abd al-Rahman. Then he said: The best of names are Abdullah and Abd al-Rahman and al-Harith."
"17751","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Ziyad or Abbad narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Umayr ibn Said, from Sabra ibn Abi Sabra, from his father, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: What are your children. He said: So-and-so and so-and-so and Abd al-Uzza. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is Abd al-Rahman. The truest of your names, or among the best of your names, if you name, are Abdullah and Abd al-Rahman and al-Harith."
"17752","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Khaythama who said: My grandfather had a boy born and named him Aziz, so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: A boy was born to me. He said: What did you name him. He said: I said: Aziz. He said: No, rather he is Abd al-Rahman. My father said: So he is."
